  "content": "Productivity, or the output per unit of labor input, is what shapes our standard of living. Primary among the factors that determine productivity growth is the rate of investment-in capital equipment, technology, and human resource development. Saving provides the funds to support that investment. To improve the rate of investment, and thereby productivity growth, saving should be raised. The basic issue is one of reallocating resources away from current consumption and toward investment in the future. Evidence of the relationship between a nation's rate of saving and its growth of productivity is shown in exhibit 1.",
  "description": null,
  "id": 6,
  "type": "text"
}
---
{
  "bbox": [
