      ],
      "page_id": 17
    }
  ],
  "content": "The personal saving rate (saving as a share of after-tax income of households) was also a major source of the weakness in national saving during the past decade. The personal saving rate has fallen from an average of 7.2 percent in the 1950 to 1979 period to a post-Depression low of 2.9 percent by 1987. Personal saving has since risen to 5 percent of disposable personal income in early 1990 but still remains well below the long-term average, as shown in exhibit 3.",
  "description": null,
  "id": 14,
  "type": "text"
}
